[statement]
A regular file's device major field of two spaces, a NUL, a space and
digits, after another member. GNU tar does not read a regular file's
device fields, bsdtar and Python read zero, and Go reads the digits,
which name no device on a regular file. ferrotape reads the member, as
every reader does.

[archive]
header name=first
data "1\n"
header name=odd devmajor="  \x00 0010"
header name=after
end

[verdict]
all: read

